er rather than a cascade path. Temporally, 303's first event falls in [47196,47495] and its second in [52896,53195] (steps 08, 11). Two of 1293's events (~[42996,43895] and ~[44796,45695]) precede any 303 activity, and its last event (~[51096,52895]) precedes 303's second event (steps 09, 12). The only 1293 event after 303's first emission lies in [47496,48395], and it is NOT the 28\u21921293 edge (step_15), so the sole candidate bridging path is ruled out; any alternative would require >=3 unobserved intermediate hops squeezed into ~300 time units. Hub 28's activity in that stretch (step_16) is background traffic unrelated to 1293. No 600-unit-gap time-respecting chain from 303 to 1293 exists."}, "raw_final_response": "```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_9a5aa702\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [303, 1293],\n  \"window\": [40296, 54695],\n  \"confidence\": 0.72,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_16\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"Both endpoints are very sparse in the window: 303 has only 2 events (both outgoing, to 1409 and 1465; steps 02, 10) and 1293 has 4 events with neighbours {28, 726, 1438, 1574} (steps 02, 05). Structurally, none of 1293's neighbours appears in 303's 2-hop neighbourhood (step_03: {1409,1465,2,97,157,214,960,1056,1141,1224,1555,1612,1925}), so the static distance from 303 to 1293 is at least 4 hops; the only visible bridge is the hub 28 (step_04), whose huge fan-out is a volume confounder 